lesson k-zigzags-and-waves v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=1 subject=writing levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Zigzags and waves"
  goal "Draw straight, zigzag and wavy lines from left to right, and find those lines inside letters."

  look {
    scene 26x17 {
      lines row kinds=["straight", "zigzag", "wavy"] colour=blue at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      A straight line, a zigzag with sharp points, and a wavy line that goes up and down smoothly.
      Draw each one from left to right, the way we write. These lines are hiding inside letters: w
      is a zigzag, and s is a wave.
      """
  }
  do {
    show k.trace-a-line x="zigzag"
    level easy {
      worked k.line-kind x="straight" level=medium
    }
    practice k.line-kind count=2 seed=2
    practice k.which-line count=2 seed=3
    show k.trace-a-line x="wavy"
    practice k.line-in-letter count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.zigzag-letter k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.draw-waves
  }
  remember {
    say "Draw from left to right. Zigzags have points, and waves are smooth."
  }

  grown-ups """
    These are the strokes that letters are built from, and the traced lines are for you to look
    at: watch that the line goes from left to right and keeps its shape. Big movements come before
    small ones, so if the pencil wobbles, draw the lines in the air with a whole arm first, then on
    a big sheet with a crayon. Off the page, draw zigzag mountains and wavy seas in chalk or with a
    stick in sand. England, Reception, ELG Fine Motor Skills (recalled, not fetched): "Use a range
    of small tools, including scissors, paint brushes and cutlery".
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level a straight line is named in the teacher's pen first, the lines to find are the zigzag and the straight one, and the letters are l and w."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the lines to find are the wave and the spiral, the letters are z and s, and the two-star letter is v."
  }
}
